#edb/ref 1069 "q-343690" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495094 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495094 #edb/ref 1071 "A particle of mass $0.8\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. An external periodic force \n\n$$\nF(t)=(4{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{5}{2}t)-2)\\,\\text{N}\n$$\n\nis applied to the particle.\n\nThe position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds. If the particle moves with forced harmonic motion without damping and the system experiences resonance, what is the spring constant $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}${\\text{kg/s}}^{2}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495094 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "64d62ce0-8437-5a77-8100-0fa04bf9d1d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495094 #edb/ref 1074 "The equation of motion for a particle of mass $m$ moving with forced harmonic motion without damping under the action of a spring with spring constant $k$ and external force $F(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-ky+F(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m$ and $F(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n0.8{y}^{″}=-ky+(4{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{5}{2}t)-2).\n$$\n\nSimplifying and rearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{5k}{4}y=\\frac{5}{2}(2{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{5}{2}t)-1).\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ here represents simple harmonic motion, and it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants of integration, and $\\omega $ is the system's internal frequency.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{5k}{4}\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{4}{5}{\\omega }^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe oscillator experiences resonance when the frequency of the external periodic force $f(t)=\\frac{5}{2}(2{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{5}{2}t)-1)$ is equal to the frequency of the complementary solution $\\omega .$ Since\n\n$$\nf(t)=\\frac{5}{2}(2{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{5}{2}t)-1)=\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t),\n$$\n\nthe frequency of the external periodic force is $5.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{4}{5}{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot {5}^{2}=20\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495178 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186495252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495178 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "04593abc-de35-5ea9-a146-5ea660c1a706" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495178 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186495094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495189 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186495200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495189 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2265a2b8-a125-50ed-bfc1-8d6afde6c2a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495189 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186335729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495200 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186495206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495200 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3fe268b2-a12f-5127-8880-a5efc009faa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495200 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186357702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495206 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186495178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495206 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "683c98ce-5d82-50d3-a3f8-d24ea690b317" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495206 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186317420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495252 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c95a38fe-1860-539e-b737-8be81b3f72b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495252 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517486 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517486 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517486 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517486 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517486 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517486 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517486 #edb/ref 1045 "Resonance in Vibrating Systems" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517486 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186518259 #edb/ref 175921860454